00:01:51.822 --> 00:01:57.102
A reminder that evaluation entry can still deliver when the catalyst actually shows follow-through.

00:01:57.922 --> 00:02:02.622
Consensus estimates are the raw material for a beat screen, not a headline to cheer.

00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:08.422
This season also shows 60 companies growing EPS year over year, which is a different test

00:02:08.422 --> 00:02:13.762
than beating a forecast, and 48 of the 76 beat revenue estimates on top of that.

00:02:14.242 --> 00:02:15.822
The practical filter is simple.

00:02:16.362 --> 00:02:22.782
Demand at least three prior EPS beats, require revenue growth above 5%, then layer the revenue

00:02:22.782 --> 00:02:27.222
beat history so you are not buying a company that only manufactured a bottom line surprise.

00:02:27.982 --> 00:02:32.922
You pull that in a brokerage watch list, or a free screener such as FinViz by setting EPS

00:02:32.922 --> 00:02:37.682
surprise filters, and sorting by the next announcement date, and you do it before you

00:02:37.682 --> 00:02:43.022
size anything. Picture a contractor you only rehire after three jobs came in under budget

00:02:43.022 --> 00:02:47.782
and the invoices kept getting larger. One lucky under budget week is not a pattern,

00:02:48.342 --> 00:02:53.602
and one EPS beat is not a streak. What would you do with a name that has three EPS beats

00:02:53.602 --> 00:02:58.742
and a revenue miss? I would leave it off the list until the top line confirms, because

00:02:58.742 --> 00:03:03.822
the two metric cross check is what cuts false positives. The screen has had edge when the

00:03:03.822 --> 00:03:08.282
post-release tape confirms the beat, and it has failed in prior quarters when sector

00:03:08.282 --> 00:03:11.362
rotation dumped growth names that had just printed good numbers.

00:03:12.022 --> 00:03:14.462
Remember, screen for a streak, not a headline.

00:03:15.122 --> 00:03:19.402
That same insistence on a real earnings gate is what we are about to put on a simulated

00:03:19.402 --> 00:03:24.282
lithium name, and it is also how you keep from treating every preview as a must-trade.

